                                "sense_id": "ea6a5fb4-5050-383a-853e-93341065ddfc",
                                "text": "To John Foxe, his honoured Father, the faithfull Martyrologian[…]a most disert searcher into the Antiquities of Histories[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6a85854-81de-418b-ad9a-649fcd1e98cd",
                                "sense_id": "ea6a5fb4-5050-383a-853e-93341065ddfc",
                                "text": "[…]not that they are better, or more disert and eloquent than those [sc. books] of this learned Scotchman[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "10200895-e366-49bc-b583-684d2b362ff2",
                                "sense_id": "ea6a5fb4-5050-383a-853e-93341065ddfc",
                                "text": "[…]for whence[…]can they better derive the Principles of that Science, than from this most Disert Poet[…]"
                            }
                        ]
